\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  My God, how wonderful Thou art,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Thy majesty how bright!
\par How beautiful Thy mercy seat,
\par In depts of burning light!
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  How dread are Thy eternal years,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 O everlasting Lord,
\par By prostrate spirits day and night
\par Incessantly adored!
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  O how I fear Thee, living God,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj With deepest, tenderest fears,
\par And worship Thee, with trembling hope
\par   And penitential tears!
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   4.   Yet I may love Thee too, O Lord,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0  Almighty as Thou are,
\par For Thou have stooped to ask of me
\par \pard\li144\sl190\slmult0      The love of my poor heart.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  5.    No earthly father loves likeThee;
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0    No mother e'er so  mild,
\par    Bears and forebears  as Thou have done
\par   With me Thy sinful child
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  6.  How beautiful, how beautiful,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj     The sight of Thee must be,
\par    Thy endless wisdom, boundless power,
\par \pard         And awful purity!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

